/-!
# The numbers |2^i - 3^j| up to a(3000) of A014121 (OEIS A014121 and A363999)

Self-contained; depends on Mathlib only. Part of the AcceleratedCollatz Lean 4 project.

A number v is a term of A014121 when v = |2^i - 3^j| for some i, j ≥ 0, and of A363999
when for some i, j ≥ 1 (`IsPowDiff`). Up to N = 328256967394000206715, the 3000th term of
A014121, both are given by one table of 3000 witnesses (v, i, j) (`witnesses`), with
i, j ≥ 1 where possible:

* A014121: v ≤ N is a term exactly when v ∈ `table0` (`a014121_iff`), 3000 numbers in
  increasing order (`table0_length`, `table0_sorted`): the table of Kevin Ryde in A014121,
  "Conjectured table of n, a(n) for n = 1..3000", is right.
* A363999: v ≤ N is a term exactly when v ∈ `table1` (`a363999_iff`), 2891 numbers in
  increasing order (`table1_length`, `table1_sorted`).

The proof is a congruence sieve, without bounds for linear forms in logarithms. With
M = 2^8 3^3 5 7 13 17 19 37 73 97 109 193 433 577 1153, the orders of 2 and 3 modulo these
primes divide 288 and 1728, so for i ≥ 8 the residue of 2^i mod M has period 288 in i, and
for j ≥ 3 that of 3^j has period 1728 in j (`two_pow_modEq`, `three_pow_modEq`). So for
i ≥ 8, j ≥ 3 the residue of 2^i - 3^j mod M is one of the 288·1728 residues of i < 296,
j < 1731, and a kernel check of these (`regionOK`, in 144 parts of 2 classes of i) shows
that each of them within N of 0 (mod M) is in `table1`. Since 2N < M, the residue gives the
number. The rest, i < 8 or j < 3, has i < 69 and j < 44 below N (`smallRow`, one check per i).
-/

namespace PowDiff

/-- v = |2^i - 3^j| for some i, j ≥ lo. -/
def IsPowDiff (lo v : ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∃ i j, lo ≤ i ∧ lo ≤ j ∧ ((2 : ℤ) ^ i - 3 ^ j).natAbs = v

/-- |x - y| in ℕ. -/
def D (x y : ℕ) : ℕ := x - y + (y - x)

theorem natAbs_eq_D (i j : ℕ) : ((2 : ℤ) ^ i - 3 ^ j).natAbs = D (2 ^ i) (3 ^ j) := by
  unfold D
  rcases le_total (3 ^ j) (2 ^ i) with h | h
  · have e : (2 : ℤ) ^ i - 3 ^ j = ((2 ^ i - 3 ^ j : ℕ) : ℤ) := by push_cast [Nat.cast_sub h]; ring
    rw [e, Int.natAbs_natCast, Nat.sub_eq_zero_of_le h, Nat.add_zero]
  · have e : (2 : ℤ) ^ i - 3 ^ j = -((3 ^ j - 2 ^ i : ℕ) : ℤ) := by push_cast [Nat.cast_sub h]; ring
    rw [e, Int.natAbs_neg, Int.natAbs_natCast, Nat.sub_eq_zero_of_le h, Nat.zero_add]

